@lang en
-- Independent tests for the Interpretation Act 2005 (Ireland) encoding.
-- Written by an independent test author. Expected values come from ANSWERS.md (written from the source text BEFORE any .l4 was opened).
-- Scenario numbers S<n> are the numbers in ANSWERS.md. A line "GAP" means the encoding has no function that can be asked the scenario.
-- Where the encoding signals "not covered" it does so by REFUSE, so those scenarios are asserted with #ASSERT REFUSED.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ie-general`
IMPORT `ie-operation-and-construction`
IMPORT `ie-words-and-meaning`
IMPORT `ie-citation-and-text`
IMPORT `ie-powers-and-service`
IMPORT `ie-powers-duties-continuing`
IMPORT `ie-repeal`
IMPORT `ie-schedule-definitions`
IMPORT `ie-acts-referred-to`

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a document`
`td` a b c d e f MEANS
    `Facts about a document` WITH
        `it is an Act of the Oireachtas`                                                                                        IS a
        `it is a statute that was in force in Saorstat Eireann immediately before the Constitution came into operation`         IS b
        `it continued in force by virtue of Article 50 of the Constitution`                                                     IS c
        `it is an order, regulation, rule, bye-law, warrant, licence, certificate, direction, notice, guideline or other like document` IS d
        `it was made, issued, granted or otherwise created by or under an Act or such an instrument`                            IS e
        `it is a portion of an Act or of a statutory instrument`                                                                IS f

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of enactment`
      c IS A `What an enactment says about its own commencement`
      d IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment`
`tf` k c d MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment` WITH
        `its kind`                         IS k
        `what it says about commencement`  IS c
        `the day of its passing or making` IS d

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where a contrary intention appears`
`tw` a b c MEANS
    `Where a contrary intention appears` WITH
        `in this Act`                         IS a
        `in the enactment itself`             IS b
        `in the Act under which it is made`   IS c

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for the savings in section 3(2)`
`ts` a b c d MEANS
    `Facts for the savings in section 3(2)` WITH
        `the repealed Act assigns a meaning to a word or expression in another enactment`   IS a
        `the repealed Act provides for another matter in another enactment`                  IS b
        `without that provision in this Act the other enactment would be changed in intent or become unclear or absurd`     IS c
        `applying to the other enactment the corresponding provision of this Act would change it in intent or make it unclear or absurd` IS d

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of enactment`
      penal IS A BOOLEAN
      obscure IS A BOOLEAN
      absurd IS A BOOLEAN
      fails IS A BOOLEAN
      known IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The provision to be construed`
`tp` k penal obscure absurd fails known MEANS
    `The provision to be construed` WITH
        `where it is found`                                                IS k
        `it relates to the imposition of a penal or other sanction`        IS penal
        `it is obscure or ambiguous`                                       IS obscure
        `on a literal interpretation it would be absurd`                   IS absurd
        `on a literal interpretation it would fail to reflect the plain intention` IS fails
        `the plain intention can be ascertained`                           IS known

GIVEN passed IS A DATE
      changed IS A DATE
      relevant IS A BOOLEAN
      permit IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A change since a provision was made`
`tchg` passed changed relevant permit MEANS
    `A change since a provision was made` WITH
        `the day the Act was passed or the instrument was made`   IS passed
        `the day of the change`                                   IS changed
        `the change is in the law, social conditions, technology, the meaning of words used, or another relevant matter` IS relevant
        `the text, purpose and context of the provision permit the allowance` IS permit

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for section 8`
`t8` a b c d e MEANS
    `Facts for section 8` WITH
        `the first Act or portion of an Act provides that summary proceedings for offences under it may be prosecuted by a specified person` IS a
        `it is subsequently read together as one with a provision of another Act`                                                          IS b
        `an offence is created under that provision which can be prosecuted in a summary manner`                                           IS c
        `no express power is given to the specified person to so prosecute`                                                                IS d
        `some other person is authorised by that other Act to bring such proceedings`                                                      IS e

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about an Act for citing it`
`tc` a b c MEANS
    `Facts about an Act for citing it` WITH
        `citing it by number and year is appropriate`                                                           IS a
        `it was passed prior to the enactment of the Constitution of the Irish Free State (Saorstat Eireann) Act 1922` IS b
        `there was more than one parliamentary session in the same regnal year`                                 IS c

GIVEN e IS A DATE
      p IS A DATE
      fixed IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A BOOLEAN
      needed IS A BOOLEAN
      restricted IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for section 17`
`tx` e p fixed power needed restricted MEANS
    `Facts for section 17` WITH
        `the day on which the Act or provision is expressed to come into operation`   IS e
        `the day of the passing of the Act`                                            IS p
        `the day on which it comes into operation is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner` IS fixed
        `the Act confers a power to make a statutory instrument or do an act or thing for the purposes of the Act or provision`           IS power
        `the making or doing of it is necessary or expedient to enable the Act or provision to have full force and effect immediately on its coming into operation` IS needed
        `a restriction imposed by the Act forbids doing it on the day in question`   IS restricted

GIVEN day IS A DATE
      after1976 IS A BOOLEAN
      under IS A BOOLEAN
      outside IS A BOOLEAN
      recognised IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about an adopted child`
`tch` day after1976 under outside recognised MEANS
    `Facts about an adopted child` WITH
        `the day the Act was passed`                                                                    IS day
        `the Act was passed after the passing of the Adoption Act 1976`                                  IS after1976
        `the child was adopted by the person under the Adoption Acts 1952 to 1998 or another enactment to be construed together with them` IS under
        `the child was adopted outside the State`                                                       IS outside
        `the adoption is recognised by virtue of the law for the time being in force in the State`      IS recognised

GIVEN e IS A NUMBER
      n IS A NUMBER
      a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Point
`tpt` e n a MEANS
    Point WITH
        `east of the origin` IS e
        `north of the origin` IS n
        `above the origin`   IS a

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      u IS A `Unit of time`
      how IS A `How a period is counted`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A period of time`
`tpd` n u how d MEANS
    `A period of time` WITH
        `its length`                   IS n
        `its unit`                     IS u
        `how it is counted`            IS how
        `the day it is counted from`   IS d

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A document sent by post`
`tpo` a b c d e MEANS
    `A document sent by post` WITH
        `an enactment authorises or requires the document to be served by post, by the word serve, give, deliver, send or any other word` IS a
        `the letter was properly addressed`                                       IS b
        `prepayment is required`                                                  IS c
        `the letter was prepaid`                                                  IS d
        `a letter containing the document was posted`                             IS e

GIVEN p IS A STRING
      f IS A DATE
      l IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `A holder of an office`
`th` p f l MEANS
    `A holder of an office` WITH
        person       IS p
        `first day`  IS f
        `last day`   IS l

`holders` MEANS
    LIST (`th` "Alice" (YMD 2020 1 1) (JUST (YMD 2024 6 30))), (`th` "Bob" (YMD 2024 7 1) NOTHING)

GIVEN day IS A DATE
      req IS A BOOLEAN
      used IS A NUMBER
      ceased IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An occasion on which an enactment, a power or a duty may be called on`
`to` day req used ceased MEANS
    `An occasion on which an enactment, a power or a duty may be called on` WITH
        `the day of the occasion`                                                   IS day
        `the occasion requires it`                                                  IS req
        `the number of earlier occasions on which it has already been used`         IS used
        `the enactment has ceased to have effect before that day`                   IS ceased

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE DATE
      b IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts for full age`
`tfa` a b MEANS
    `Facts for full age` WITH
        `the day on which the person attained the age of 18 years` IS a
        `the day on which the person married`                      IS b

GIVEN began IS A DATE
      ended IS A MAYBE DATE
      kind IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about proceedings at a repeal`
`tpr` began ended kind MEANS
    `Facts about proceedings at a repeal` WITH
        `the day the proceedings began`   IS began
        `the day the proceedings ended`   IS ended
        `they are in respect of a right, privilege, obligation, liability, offence or contravention of the kind in (c) and (d)` IS kind

`the Act as passed on 2025-03-10 and silent` MEANS `tf` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` (JUST (YMD 2025 3 10))

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t is a Sunday` d MEANS
    `Weekday of` d EQUALS 0

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t no day is a holiday` d MEANS
    FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t only 2025-12-26 is a holiday` d MEANS
    d EQUALS YMD 2025 12 26

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t only 2025-10-27 is a holiday` d MEANS
    d EQUALS YMD 2025 10 27

§ `Part 1: ss 1 to 4`

-- S1 GAP: s1(1) short title: no function for a permitted short title.
-- S2 s1(2) L84: the day this Act is expressed to come into operation.
#ASSERT `the day on which the enactment comes into operation, as the text names it` `the facts about this Act` EQUALS YMD 2006 1 1
-- S3 s1(2) + s16(2) L84,156: the moment this Act comes into operation is the end of 2005-12-31.
#ASSERT (`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` `the facts about this Act`)'s `the day it ends` EQUALS YMD 2005 12 31
-- S4 s1(2) + s16(2): not in operation at noon on 2005-12-31 (the encoding works in whole days: "throughout the day").
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` `the facts about this Act` `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2005 12 31)
-- S5 s1(2) + s16(2): in operation at noon on 2006-01-01.
#ASSERT `the enactment` `the facts about this Act` `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2006 1 1)
-- S6 GAP: 23:59:59 on 2005-12-31 is a time of day; the encoding answers whole days only.
-- S7 s2(1) "Act" (a) L87
#ASSERT `is an Act` (`td` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S8 s2(1) "Act" (b) L88
#ASSERT `is an Act` (`td` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S9 s2(1) "Act" (b) L88: Saorstat statute repealed before the Constitution (so not in force immediately before it).
#ASSERT NOT `is an Act` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S10 s2(1) "Act" (b) L88: a British statute in force in Saorstat Eireann and continued by Article 50.
#ASSERT `is an Act` (`td` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S11 s2(1) "Act" L86-88: a British statute never in force in Saorstat Eireann.
#ASSERT NOT `is an Act` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S12 s2(1) "Act" L86-88: a statutory instrument is not an Act.
#ASSERT NOT `is an Act` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- S13 s2(1) "enactment" L89: a statutory instrument is an enactment.
#ASSERT `is an enactment` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- S14 s2(1) "enactment" L89: a portion of an Act.
#ASSERT `is an enactment` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- S15 s2(1) "enactment" L89: a Bill is not an enactment.
#ASSERT NOT `is an enactment` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S16 s2(1) "repeal" L90: revoke.
#ASSERT `the word is a repeal within the Act` revoke
-- S17 s2(1) "repeal" L90: rescind.
#ASSERT `the word is a repeal within the Act` rescind
-- S18 s2(1) "repeal" L90: abrogate.
#ASSERT `the word is a repeal within the Act` abrogate
-- S19 s2(1) "repeal" L90: cancel.
#ASSERT `the word is a repeal within the Act` cancel
-- S20 s2(1) "repeal" L90: suspend is not listed; not covered.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the word is a repeal within the Act` `some other word`
-- S21 s2(1) "statutory instrument" L91: a licence granted under an Act.
#ASSERT `is a statutory instrument` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- S22 s2(1) "statutory instrument" L91: a warrant issued under an Act.
#ASSERT `is a statutory instrument` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- S23 s2(1) "statutory instrument" L91: a guideline made under an Act.
#ASSERT `is a statutory instrument` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- S24 s2(1) "statutory instrument" L91: a bye-law made under an Act.
#ASSERT `is a statutory instrument` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- S25 s2(1) "statutory instrument" L91: a direction issued under a regulation made under an Act.
#ASSERT `is a statutory instrument` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- S26 s2(1) "statutory instrument" L91: a private contract.
#ASSERT NOT `is a statutory instrument` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S27 s2(1) "statutory instrument" L91: a notice issued by a body with no Act behind it.
#ASSERT NOT `is a statutory instrument` (`td` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- S28 s2(2) L92: expired.
#ASSERT `for the purposes of this Act the enactment is deemed to have been repealed` `it has expired`
-- S29 s2(2) L92: replaced.
#ASSERT `for the purposes of this Act the enactment is deemed to have been repealed` `it has been replaced`
-- S30 s2(2) L92: lapsed.
#ASSERT `for the purposes of this Act the enactment is deemed to have been repealed` `it has lapsed`
-- S31 s2(2) L92: still in force.
#ASSERT NOT `for the purposes of this Act the enactment is deemed to have been repealed` `it still has effect`
-- S32 s3(1)(a) L94
#ASSERT `section 3(1) lists the Act` `the Interpretation Act 1889`
-- S33 s3(1)(b) L95
#ASSERT `section 3(1) lists the Act` `the Interpretation Act 1923`
-- S34 s3(1)(c) L96
#ASSERT `section 3(1) lists the Act` `the Interpretation Act 1937`
-- S35 s3(1)(d) L97
#ASSERT `section 3(1) lists the Act` `the Interpretation (Amendment) Act 1993`
-- S36 s3(1) L93-97: an Act not listed (the Statutory Declarations Act 1938).
#ASSERT NOT `section 3(1) lists the Act` `another Act`
-- S37 s3(2)(a) L98-101: absence of the meaning would change the other enactment's intent.
#ASSERT `the repeal does not affect the meaning assigned` (`ts` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- S38 s3(2)(a)(ii) L100-101: applying this Act's meaning would make the other enactment absurd.
#ASSERT `the repeal does not affect the meaning assigned` (`ts` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- S39 s3(2)(a) L101: unclear only.
#ASSERT `the repeal does not affect the meaning assigned` (`ts` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- S40 s3(2)(a) L98-101: neither route changes the other enactment.
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect the meaning assigned` (`ts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S41 s3(2)(b) L102-105: a matter other than a meaning; its absence would make the other enactment absurd.
#ASSERT `the repeal does not affect the matter provided for` (`ts` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- S42 s3(2)(b)(ii) L104-105: this Act provides a corresponding matter and nothing changes.
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect the matter provided for` (`ts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- S43 s3(2)(b) L102: a matter that is the assigning of a meaning is governed by (a), not (b).
#ASSERT NOT `the repeal does not affect the matter provided for` (`ts` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- S44 s4(1) L106: contrary intention in the enactment itself.
#ASSERT NOT `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` (`tw` FALSE TRUE NOTHING)
-- S45 s4(1) L106: contrary intention in the Act under which the SI is made.
#ASSERT NOT `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` (`tw` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE))
-- S46 s4(1) L106: contrary intention only in an unrelated Act (none of the three places).
#ASSERT `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` (`tw` FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
-- S47 GAP: s4(1) "in so far as": the function is all-or-nothing and has no partial-disapplication input.
-- S48 s4(2) L107: no contrary intention in this Act.
#ASSERT `a provision of this Act that relates to other Acts applies also to this Act` FALSE
-- S49 s4(2) L107: a contrary intention in this Act.
#ASSERT NOT `a provision of this Act that relates to other Acts applies also to this Act` TRUE

§ `Part 2: ss 5 to 12`

-- S50 s5(1) L109-114: obscure, non-penal, intention ascertainable.
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`tp` `an Act of the Oireachtas` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the Oireachtas`
-- S51 s5(1)(b) L111: literal reading absurd.
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`tp` `an Act of the Oireachtas` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the Oireachtas`
-- S52 s5(1)(b) L111: literal reading fails to reflect the plain intention.
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`tp` `an Act of the Oireachtas` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the Oireachtas`
-- S53 s5(1) L109: penal provision.
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`tp` `an Act of the Oireachtas` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `section 5 does not apply`
-- S54 s5(1) L109: "other sanction" (a forfeiture) is also excluded.
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`tp` `an Act of the Oireachtas` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `section 5 does not apply`
-- S55 s5(1) L110-111: a clear provision whose literal reading is neither absurd nor contrary to intention.
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`tp` `an Act of the Oireachtas` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `section 5 does not apply`
-- S56 s5(1) L114: ambiguous but the intention cannot be ascertained from the Act as a whole.
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`tp` `an Act of the Oireachtas` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `section 5 gives no direction because the plain intention cannot be ascertained`
-- S57 s5(1)(b)(i) L112: whose intention for an Act of the Oireachtas.
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`tp` `an Act of the Oireachtas` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the Oireachtas`
-- S58 s5(1)(b)(ii) L113: whose intention for a Saorstat Eireann statute.
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`tp` `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the parliament concerned`
-- S59 s5(2) L115-118: a non-penal SI provision.
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`tp` `a statutory instrument` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the maker of the instrument`
-- S60 s5(2) L115: a penal SI provision.
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`tp` `a statutory instrument` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `section 5 does not apply`
-- S61 s5(2) L118: whose intention governs an SI.
#ASSERT `what section 5 directs about` (`tp` `a statutory instrument` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `construe to reflect the plain intention` `the maker of the instrument`
-- S62 s6 L119: technology changed since passing, text permits.
#ASSERT `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`tchg` (YMD 2000 1 1) (YMD 2010 1 1) TRUE TRUE)
-- S63 s6 L119: text does not permit.
#ASSERT NOT `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`tchg` (YMD 2000 1 1) (YMD 2010 1 1) TRUE FALSE)
-- S64 s6 L119: applies to a statutory instrument (the record says "passed or made").
#ASSERT `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`tchg` (YMD 2020 5 12) (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE TRUE)
-- S65 s6 L119: applies to a penal provision too (s6 has no penal input at all).
#ASSERT `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`tchg` (YMD 2000 1 1) (YMD 2010 1 1) TRUE TRUE)
-- S66 s6 L119: the change occurred before the Act was passed.
#ASSERT NOT `a court may make allowance for the change in construing the provision` (`tchg` (YMD 2000 1 1) (YMD 1999 1 1) TRUE TRUE)
-- S67 GAP: s6 "may" (permission, not duty): the function yields a boolean "may" and has no way to ask "must".
-- S68 s7(1) L120: for s5 or s6, marginal notes accompanying the enrolled text of an Act.
#ASSERT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` `an Act of the Oireachtas` TRUE TRUE
-- S69 s7(1) L120: for a purpose other than s5 or s6.
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` `an Act of the Oireachtas` FALSE TRUE
-- S70 s7(1) L120: an SI construed under s5(2).
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` `a statutory instrument` TRUE TRUE
-- S71 s7(1)(a) L121: the enrolled text of an Act of the Oireachtas.
#ASSERT `the text of an Act that section 7(1) names for` `an Act of the Oireachtas, paragraph (a)` EQUALS `the signed text as enrolled for record in the Office of the Registrar of the Supreme Court pursuant to Article 25.4.5 of the Constitution`
-- S72 s7(1)(b) L122: the enrolled text of a Saorstat Eireann Act.
#ASSERT `the text of an Act that section 7(1) names for` `an Act of the Oireachtas of Saorstat Eireann, paragraph (b)` EQUALS `the signed text as enrolled for record in the office of the officer of the Supreme Court of Saorstat Eireann whom Dail Eireann determined pursuant to Article 42 of the Constitution of the Irish Free State`
-- S73 s7(2) L124: presumption of a copy of an Act required to be judicially noticed.
#ASSERT `it is presumed that the copy is a copy of the text to which section 7(1) relates` TRUE FALSE
-- S74 s7(2) L124: the contrary is shown.
#ASSERT NOT `it is presumed that the copy is a copy of the text to which section 7(1) relates` TRUE TRUE
-- S75 s8 L125-131: all conditions met.
#ASSERT `section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` (`t8` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- S76 s8 L131: another person is authorised.
#ASSERT NOT `section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` (`t8` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- S77 s8(b) L130: the other Act already gives the specified person the power.
#ASSERT NOT `section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` (`t8` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- S78 s8(b) L130: the offence cannot be prosecuted summarily.
#ASSERT NOT `section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` (`t8` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- S79 s8(a)(ii) L128: not read together with the other Act.
#ASSERT NOT `section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` (`t8` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- S80 s8(a) L126: "whenever passed" (the record has no passing-order input; the conditions are met).
#ASSERT `section 8 lets the specified person bring summary proceedings for the offence` (`t8` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- S81 s9(1) L132: "section".
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` section EQUALS `a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs`
-- S82 s9(1) L132: "Part" in an SI.
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` Part EQUALS `a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs`
-- S83 s9(2) L133: "paragraph".
#ASSERT `a reference to a division is read as a reference to a division of` paragraph EQUALS `a division of the provision in which the reference occurs`
-- S84 GAP: s9 with s4(1) contrary intention: the s9 function takes no contrary-intention input.
-- S85 s10 L134
#ASSERT `an enactment may be applied on the occasion` (`to` (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE 3 FALSE)
-- S86 s11(b) L137: heading "Example" at the end of a provision.
#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` Example `, included as stated by` TRUE EQUALS `the example is not exhaustive of the provision and may extend, but does not limit, its meaning`
-- S87 s11(a) L136: heading "Sampla".
#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` Sampla `, included as stated by` TRUE EQUALS `the example is not exhaustive of the provision and may extend, but does not limit, its meaning`
-- S88 s11 L135-138: heading "Illustration".
#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` `some other heading` `, included as stated by` TRUE EQUALS `section 11 does not apply`
-- S89 s11 L138: heading "Examples" in a schedule relating to the provision.
#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` Examples `, included as stated by` TRUE EQUALS `the example is not exhaustive of the provision and may extend, but does not limit, its meaning`
-- S90 s11(ii) L140: may extend the meaning (the one constructor says "may extend, but does not limit").
#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` Example `, included as stated by` TRUE EQUALS `the example is not exhaustive of the provision and may extend, but does not limit, its meaning`
-- S91 s11(ii) L140: may not limit the meaning (same constructor).
#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` Example `, included as stated by` TRUE EQUALS `the example is not exhaustive of the provision and may extend, but does not limit, its meaning`
-- S92 s11 L138: an example in the middle of a provision.
#ASSERT `the effect of an example under the heading` Example `, included as stated by` FALSE EQUALS `section 11 does not apply`
-- S93 s12 L141: neither material nor misleading.
